NAME
    wmhello - sample WM client (Path C phase 6)

SYNOPSIS
    wmhello [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Demonstrates the smallest possible client of the session-112
    WM protocol. Opens a 220x140 window via SYS_WM_CREATE, paints
    a moving colored square + animated background, presents the
    surface to wmd each frame, and exits after SECONDS (default 10).

    The compositor must be running first. Typical usage:

       (start `wmd 30` in one shell)
       wmhello 8           # opens, animates, closes

    The window appears with a cyan title bar containing the title
    "wmhello"; wmd places it at a deterministic per-client offset.

EXIT STATUS
    0  on normal exit (timer elapsed, window closed)
    1  if SYS_WM_CREATE fails — usually means no wmd is running

SEE ALSO
    wmd(1), gfx(1), mouse(1)
